  "evidence": "Read the two selected suppliers for SInv and SWtOdd and followed the derivative of the matrix congruence, the Stokes argument, the place-permutation tensor span and the odd-degree filter to its stable rank application. The degree-three calculation uses independent Hermitian matrices.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "IVF-01",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "An archimedean invariant form integrates to a closed cochain",
      "anchor": "inputs-invariant-forms",
      "statement": "A form of degree m on tuples of positive Hermitian matrices invariant under every archimedean change of basis is smooth on the cone and has zero exterior derivative. Its simplex cochain vanishes on boundaries. This supplies the closedness used for the mean-zero remainder.",
      "hypotheses": "The action at each place is inverse-adjoint congruence. Each matrix in the tuple is positive definite. Tangent arguments are Hermitian. The form takes values in alternating real multilinear maps. The simplex cochain uses the positive convex cone and its Stokes identity.",
      "definitions": [
        "ω(x²)(xY₁x,…,xYₘx)=ω(I)(Y₁,…,Yₘ)",
        "Dω_I[X] is minus one half the sum of insertions of XYⱼ+YⱼX",
        "Good includes continuity on the cone and the vanishing of the simplex coboundary"
      ],
      "equations": [
        "inputs-invariant-derivative"
      ],
      "dependencies": [
        "FMA-02"
      ],
