    {
      "id": "IVF-02",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "Trace cycles give block weights and one real test per place in odd degree",
      "anchor": "inputs-invariant-trace-span",
      "statement": "After alternation the invariant tensors are spanned by products of traces indexed by permutations and places on the cycles. Each permutation cycle has one free block index, so a pattern with j cycles scales by d^j under d repeated blocks. In positive odd degree one real functional per place spans the one-cycle contributions. All weights at least two vanish on the specified filtered cycles, giving the coordinate bound for their stable homology image.",
      "hypotheses": "The odd-rank application uses the totally complex field, the stable range and the span of the filtered cycles from SBStarOdd. The pointwise decomposition uses simultaneous placewise unitary conjugation and Hermitian tangent vectors. Variation in rank uses both stabilization by padding and block repetition.",
      "definitions": [
        "a compatible place assignment is constant on each permutation cycle",
        "one trace per cycle in the index contraction, zero for incompatible place labels",
        "reversal conjugates each single-cycle trace and has sign (−1)^{m(m−1)/2}",
        "the selected real test sums the real and imaginary alternating components, one of which is zero"
      ],
      "equations": [],
